{
  "id": "search-in-rotated-sorted-array",
  "questionId": "search-in-rotated-sorted-array",
  "slug": "search-in-rotated-sorted-array",
  "title": "Search in Rotated Sorted Array",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Binary search",
  "patterns": [
    "binary search"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "blind-75",
    "grind-75",
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "even though the whole array isn't sorted, at any binary search step, at least one of the two halves around mid IS fully sorted - can you tell which one?",
    "compare nums[left] to nums[mid]: if nums[left] <= nums[mid], the left half is sorted; otherwise the right half is sorted",
    "once you know which half is sorted, you can check with a plain range comparison whether target could be in that sorted half",
    "if target is in the sorted half's range, search there; otherwise the target (if it exists) must be in the other half - search that instead"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "trying to first find the rotation pivot in a separate pass, then binary searching, which is more complex than needed",
    "using <= vs < inconsistently when deciding which half is sorted, mishandling the case where left == mid",
    "not handling the fully-non-rotated case (already sorted) as just a special case of the same logic"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "An array of distinct integers, originally sorted in ascending order, has\nbeen rotated an unknown number of positions to the right, so it's still\nmade of two sorted runs joined together.\n\n**Given the rotated array and a target value, return the index of the target, or -1 if it isn't present.**\n\nYour solution must run faster than a plain linear scan.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 5000",
      "-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4",
      "all values in nums are unique",
      "-10^4 <= target <= 10^4"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "array is not rotated at all (pivot at index 0)",
      "target is exactly at the rotation point",
      "single-element array"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [4, 5, 6, 7, 0, 1, 2], target = 0",
        "output": "4",
        "expectedOutput": "4",
        "explanation": "the array was [0,1,2,4,5,6,7] rotated so it wraps at index 4"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [4, 5, 6, 7, 0, 1, 2], target = 3",
